<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN RECTICEL'S 1996 LOSS NARROWS SHARPLY.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN RECTICEL'S 1996 LOSS NARROWS SHARPLY.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(million Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss (excl. minorities)  38    vs    682</p>
<p>    Cons sales			   35,061    vs 32,317</p>
<p>    Pre-tax operating profit	    722    vs    333</p>
<p>Note - Recticel SA is a Belgian producer of</p>
<p>polyurethane foam products. Belgian holding company Societe</p>
<p>Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) owns 70 percent of</p>
<p>Recticel shares.</p>
<p>    Extraordinary profit		   71    vs   300 loss</p>
<p>    Cash flow			     1,375    vs   794   </p>
<p>    Pre-tax current loss		   65   vs     343</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain/loss		71   vs     300 loss</p>
<p>    Pretax profit/loss			6   vs     643 loss</p>
<p>    Cash flow			     1,375   vs     794</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		8,331   vs   8,445</p>
<p>    Net financial debt		  8,338   vs   9,424</p>
<p>    Dividend				    0   vs	 0</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax</p>
<p>+32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
